  "description": "Model 2 Emulator (ElSemi). EMULATOR.INI [Input] keys come from 'ini'. Per-game CFG\\<rom>.input files are GENERATED from the profile (format decoded from EMULATOR.EXE 1.1a and the previous owner's files): one little-endian DWORD per control slot, in the game's slot order (the 'schemas' below were extracted from the emulator's control tables), then a 2-DWORD trailer. Codes: keyboard = DirectInput scan code (< 0x100); joystick button n (1-based) = joy<<8 | (n & 0xF)<<4 | (n >> 4)<<12; hat = joy<<8 | 0x0C+{Left 0, Right 1, Up 2, Down 3}; analog axis = 0xFF000000 | joy<<8 | axisObjectIndex | 0x1000 when inverted. joy = DirectInput enumeration order (1-based). axisObjectIndex = the axis' position in the device's DirectInput OBJECT enumeration (not the DIJOYSTATE offset) - e.g. G29 on G HUB: 0 wheel, 1 clutch ('Y Axis'), 2 brake, 3 accelerator; on the old Logitech driver: 0 wheel, 1 accelerator, 2 brake. Pedals that rest high and fall when pressed (direction '-') get the invert bit.",
